// Morphagene Story A + B + C + D + E — Reel + Splice metadata + Granular
//                                       path + Synchronization (CLK / EOSG
//                                       modes) + Reel persistence.
//
// Multi-splice reel with continuous Vari-Speed playback, Organize-driven
// splice selection (with EOS-hold semantics), Sound-On-Sound recording,
// a `grain_buf_ar`-based granular layer with the full Morph staircase
// (gap → 1:1 → 2:1 → 3:1 + per-grain pan → 4:1 + per-grain pitch-up),
// Story D's clocked playback modes (Gene Shift, Time Stretch) plus the
// EOSG (End-of-Gene/Splice Gate) computation, and Story E's Reel
// persistence model — a thin .vibe wrapper around `allocate_buffer` /
// `sample` so SOS-recorded content survives hot-reload. Per
// `kb/morphagene-synthdef-plan.md` §3 (Reel/Splice/Gene hierarchy),
// §4 (UGen mapping), §6.B + §6.C + §6.D + §6.E.
//
// Story E — Reel persistence (script-tier, see `kb/morphagene-reel-howto.md`):
//   The Reel is just a script-allocated buffer wired into the synthdef's
//   `bufnum` param. `fn reel(name, frames, channels)` calls the existing
//   `allocate_buffer` Rhai API (commit 7a6eebe) — the same name → same
//   bufnum across reloads, contents persist as long as the call stays in
//   the script. A `sample()`-backed alternative (`fn reel_from_sample`)
//   is provided when you want the Reel seeded from a `.wav` (the .wav
//   reload re-seeds, so SOS overdubs are not preserved by that path —
//   use `reel(...)` for SOS-safe Reels).
//
//   Splice metadata travels with the script as a Rhai array on the Reel
//   object (`r.splices`) — no separate metadata buffer, no Rust-side
//   Reel registry. The synthdef itself still divides the Reel evenly into
//   `num_splices` regions; `splices.len()` is what the helper writes into
//   `num_splices`. Custom splice positions (uneven spacing or `.wav` cue
//   chunks) are deferred to a follow-up `vibelang-sfz` ticket that
//   extends the wav loader.
//
//   Default-array preset baking is the `morphagene_reel_fill` synthdef
//   defined below: a one-shot fill that writes a generated waveform
//   (saw / square / sine / noise / silence) into the Reel via
//   `record_buf_ar` with `loop=0` + `doneAction=2`. The fill voice frees
//   itself when the buffer is full. Re-runs on every script execution
//   that calls `reel_fill_preset` — guard with a `let _bake = false`
//   flag during normal use so SOS recordings aren't overwritten.
//
// Splice model (Story B):
//   The Reel is logically divided into `num_splices` evenly-spaced splices.
//   For splice index i: start = i · BufFrames / num_splices,
//                       end   = (i+1) · BufFrames / num_splices.
//   This matches the manual's "splices distributed evenly across Organize
//   range" property literally.
//
// Selection logic (Story B):
//   pending_idx = floor(organize · num_splices), clamped. committed_idx is
//   Latch(pending_idx, trig=eos) — a knob turn re-paints the Splice LED
//   immediately but the audible switch defers to end-of-splice. The
//   committed value is bounced through a 1-frame LocalBuf to break the
//   committed → splice_len → phasor → eos → committed feedback loop.
//
// EOS detection (Story B):
//   The playback Phasor advances `rate · buf_rate_scale` per sample inside
//   [0, splice_len). At a wrap, |Δphase| ≈ splice_len; in steady state,
//   |Δphase| = |rate|. Threshold at splice_len/2 separates the two cleanly
//   under any Vari-Speed direction. Decimated to kr for the Latch.
//
// Granular path (Story C):
//   Gene-Size in [0, 1] maps via cubic curve to gene_dur_sec ∈ [splice_len,
//   50 µs]. The granular branch uses `grain_buf_ar` (numChannels=2) with
//   per-grain Tukey/Hanning envelope, cubic interpolation, and
//   maxGrains=64 to bound CPU. Morph staircase is encoded as a piecewise
//   spawn-rate factor (0.67 → 1 → 2 → 3 → flat → 4) divided by gene_dur
//   to get the Impulse spawn frequency, lagged 5 ms ("Dynamic Enveloping").
//   Per-grain pan latches white-noise ramped in over Morph 0.55..0.85.
//   Per-grain pitch-up multiplies rate by `1 + TRand(0, pitch_amt)` ramped
//   in over Morph 0.85..1.0 with max +0.8 (≈ +10 ST). The whole-splice
//   path (Story A's Phasor+BufRd) is preserved and used when Gene-Size is
//   below a 0.02 threshold; transitions cross-fade over 5 ms via Lag on
//   the active flag.
//
// Synchronization (Story D):
//   The `clk` param accepts a kr-rate clock signal (e.g. cv_clock output
//   at 0.5 amplitude = +5 V scale). Schmidt(0.05, 0.25) cleans it; a
//   delay1+diff yields a one-sample-wide rising-edge trigger. CLK-patched
//   detection uses `amplitude_kr(clk, 0.001, 1.5)` thresholded at 0.02 —
//   the 1.5 s release tolerates clocks down to ~0.7 Hz before deciding the
//   patch is gone.
//
//   Mode select (kr, gated by clk_patched ∧ gene_size_n > 0.02):
//     - Morph ≥ 0.46  →  Time Stretch  (clock drives time; rate = pitch)
//     - Morph < 0.46  →  Gene Shift    (clock advances pos by ±gene_dur)
//   Outside this band the autonomous Impulse spawner (Story C) runs. The
//   transition is cross-faded over 5 ms via Lag on the mode flags so a
//   clock pluck-in isn't a hard click.
//
//   Spawn trigger blend:
//     spawn = autonomous_impulse · auto_mode + clk_rising · clock_mode
//   Both are audio-rate (clk_rising is k2a-promoted from kr).
//
//   Position advance (Stepper at clk_rising):
//     Time Stretch:  step = +gene_dur_frames           (forward only)
//     Gene Shift:    step = ±gene_dur_frames · sign(rate)
//   Wraps at [0, splice_len_frames). In autonomous mode this Stepper is
//   inert (step=0 ⇒ no change). The output is XFADED with the Story A/C
//   slide-offset, so autonomous mode preserves slide and clock modes use
//   the accumulated offset.
//
//   EOSG (D1) is computed as `t_delay(spawn_trig, gene_dur_sec)` followed
//   by a 5 ms `trig1` gate, scaled to 10 V. The result is held in a
//   variable (`_eosg_out`) — voice synthdefs return [left, right] only
//   today, so the EOSG is a documented internal signal. Exposing it as a
//   sidecar CV output arrives with Story E (Reel registry / persistence).
//
//   Clock-rate clamping (D4): not enforced in DSP. The plan calls for
//   warn/clip at [1/3.5 s, 18 Hz] for Time Stretch; rate measurement via
//   sweep_kr+latch was deferred — out-of-range clocks just produce coarser
//   stutter (slow) or read overruns (fast). Document for future revision.
//
// SOS recording (Story B, refactored for Story D):
//   `rec_active` was dropped to free a synthdef slot for `clk` (Rhai 10-arg
//   body cap). REC is now inferred from `sos > 0.001`:
//     sos = 0      →  not recording (Reel plays back unchanged)
//     sos > 0      →  SOS recording with that mix
//     recLevel = (1 - sos) · rec_active_internal
//     preLevel =      sos  · rec_active_internal
//   Trade-off: hardware "REC active, SOS = 0" overwrite mode requires a
//   small sos > 0.001 to engage. The fully-CCW "live only" semantic is
//   approximated by sos very close to 0. Forward-only at unit rate;
//   loop=0 hard-stops at end-of-Reel. The recorder Phasor is independent
//   of the playback Phasor so reverse Vari-Speed during SOS does not flip
//   the commit direction.
//
// Param budget — Rhai closures cap at 10 args. Dropped across stories:
//   - Story B's `shift_trig` and `splice_trig` (no runtime marker drops).
//   - Story D's `rec_active` (folded into `sos > 0`, see above).
// Stereo: the granular path delivers true stereo via grain_buf_ar's
// numChannels=2 + per-grain pan; the whole-splice branch still surfaces
// channel-0 of the stereo Reel through BufRd (mono→duplicated). The
// branch crossfade therefore widens at the Gene-Size 0.02 threshold.

define_synthdef("morphagene", |builder| {
    builder
        .param("bufnum", 0.0)
        .param("num_splices", 1.0)        // 1..300, evenly-spaced division of Reel
        .param("organize", 0.0)           // 0..1 splice select knob+CV
        .param("sos", 0.0)                // 0..1 SOS mix; > 0 also gates recording
        .param("clk", 0.0)                // kr clock signal (rising edge ≈ +5 V pulse)
        .param("vari_speed", 0.0)         // bipolar -1..+1, 0 = halt
        .param("slide", 0.0)              // 0..1 start position within splice
        .param("gene_size", 0.0)          // 0..1 grain duration (cubic; 0 = whole splice)
        .param("morph", 0.0)              // 0..1 spawn cadence + pan + pitch-up
        .param("gate", 1.0)               // synth-instance lifecycle
        .body(|bufnum, num_splices, organize, sos, clk,
               vari_speed, slide, gene_size, morph, gate| {

            // --- Reel buffer info ----------------------------------------------
            let buf_n = buf_frames_kr(bufnum);
            let buf_scale = buf_rate_scale_kr(bufnum);
            let buf_sr = buf_sample_rate_kr(bufnum);

            // --- Splice metadata buffers ---------------------------------------
            // Single 1-frame committed-idx feedback cell; clear_buf_ir zeroes it
            // at synth init so the first block starts at splice 0.
            let committed_buf = local_buf_ir(1, 1.0);
            let _z2 = clear_buf_ir(committed_buf);

            // --- Vari-Speed → rate ---------------------------------------------
            // Asymmetric cubic per the manual's "12 up / 26 down" spec; smooth
            // through zero, finer-near-center, no dead-zone needed.
            let v_pos = vari_speed.max(0.0);
            let v_neg = vari_speed.min(0.0);
            let rate = (v_pos * v_pos * v_pos) * 2.0
                     + (v_neg * v_neg * v_neg) * 4.4898;

            // --- Splice selection (Organize) -----------------------------------
            // max_idx = num_splices - 1, floored at 0.
            let max_idx = (num_splices - 1.0).max(0.0);
            // Clamp shy of 1.0 so floor(organize · num_splices) lands inside
            // [0, num_splices-1] without ever hitting num_splices itself.
            let organize_pos = clip(organize, 0.0, 0.99999) * num_splices;
            let organize_idx = floor(organize_pos);
            // Use clip_kr UGen (Dynamic arity) since max_idx is a NodeRef —
            // the hand-rolled clip(NodeRef, f64, f64) helper rejects that.
            let pending_idx = clip_kr(organize_idx, 0.0, max_idx);

            // --- Committed splice idx feedback (one-block latency) -------------
            let committed_idx = buf_rd_kr(1, committed_buf, 0.0, 0, 1);

            // Splice bounds: even spacing, computed from the committed idx.
            let splice_len_frames = buf_n / num_splices.max(1.0);
            let splice_start_frame = committed_idx * splice_len_frames;
            let splice_offset = slide * splice_len_frames;

            // --- Whole-splice playback path (Story A — Phasor + BufRd) ---------
            // Audio-rate read position is splice_start + slide_offset + phase,
            // wrapped within splice_len. BufRd cubic interpolation; mono read
            // (channel 0) duplicated below.
            let phase = phasor_ar(0.0, rate * buf_scale, 0.0, splice_len_frames, 0.0);
            let read_pos = splice_start_frame
                         + wrap_ar(phase + splice_offset, 0.0, splice_len_frames);
            let raw = buf_rd_ar(2, bufnum, read_pos, 1.0, 4.0);

            // --- EOS detection (kr) --------------------------------------------
            let phase_prev = delay1_ar(phase);
            let phase_diff = phase - phase_prev;
            let abs_diff = abs(phase_diff);
            let wrap_excess = abs_diff - splice_len_frames * 0.5;
            let eos_trig_ar = sign(wrap_excess).max(0.0);
            let eos_trig = a2k_kr(eos_trig_ar);

            // Latch pending_idx on rising EOS, write back to feedback cell.
            let new_committed = latch_kr(pending_idx, eos_trig);
            let _wrote_committed = buf_wr_kr(new_committed, committed_buf, 0.0, 0);

            // --- Gene-Size mapping (C1) ----------------------------------------
            // gene_dur_sec = mix(splice_len_sec, 50µs, gene_size_n^3).
            // Cubic shape: most of the knob travel is in long-grain territory;
            // sub-millisecond pulsar grains live in the last quarter turn.
            let gene_size_n = clip(gene_size, 0.0, 1.0);
            let gs_cubed = gene_size_n.pow(3.0);
            let splice_len_sec = splice_len_frames / buf_sr.max(1.0);
            let gene_min_sec = 50.0e-6;
            let gene_dur_sec = splice_len_sec * (1.0 - gs_cubed)
                             + gene_min_sec * gs_cubed;

            // --- Morph staircase (C3) ------------------------------------------
            // Piecewise spawn-rate factor mirroring the manual's panel arc:
            //   0.00..0.25  : 0.67 → 1.00   (gap-of-silence closing)
            //   0.25..0.50  : 1.00 → 2.00   (overlap, second instance enters)
            //   0.50..0.55  : 2.00 → 3.00   (third instance enters)
            //   0.55..0.70  : 3.00         (panning ramps in — see C4)
            //   0.70..0.85  : 3.00 → 4.00   (fourth instance enters)
            //   0.85..1.00  : 4.00 + per-grain pitch-up (see C5)
            // Each segment is a clipped ramp summed onto a 0.67 baseline.
            let morph_n = clip(morph, 0.0, 1.0);
            let r0 = clip(morph_n * 4.0, 0.0, 1.0) * 0.33;
            let r1 = clip((morph_n - 0.25) * 4.0, 0.0, 1.0);
            let r2 = clip((morph_n - 0.50) * 20.0, 0.0, 1.0);
            let r3 = clip((morph_n - 0.70) * 6.6667, 0.0, 1.0);
            let spawn_rate_factor = 0.67 + r0 + r1 + r2 + r3;

            // spawn_rate_hz = factor / gene_dur_sec, clamped to a sane ceiling
            // so the tiniest gene_dur (~50 µs) doesn't push Impulse past audio
            // rate. 4 kHz is well above any rhythmic spawn density and still
            // safely below Nyquist concerns at 48 kHz.
            let raw_rate_hz = spawn_rate_factor / gene_dur_sec.max(1.0e-6);
            let spawn_rate_hz = clip(raw_rate_hz, 0.05, 4000.0);
            // 5 ms lag on spawn rate — vibelang's stand-in for the manual's
            // "Dynamic Enveloping" smoothing of grain-rate parameter jumps.
            let smoothed_rate = lag_kr(spawn_rate_hz, 0.005);

            // --- Story D: CLK input + mode detection ---------------------------
            // Schmidt cleans the kr CLK (cv_clock outputs ≈ 0.5 amplitude at
            // +5 V; threshold 0.25 with 0.05 hysteresis catches it cleanly).
            let clk_clean = schmidt_kr(clk, 0.05, 0.25);
            let clk_prev = delay1_kr(clk_clean);
            let clk_rising_kr = (clk_clean - clk_prev).max(0.0);

            // CLK-patched: amplitude follower with a 1.5 s release tolerates
            // clock periods up to ~1.4 s (≈ 0.7 Hz) before declaring "no
            // clock" — covers the Time-Stretch range (1/3.5 s to 18 Hz)
            // comfortably. Threshold 0.02 with ×100 gain → near-binary.
            let clk_env = amplitude_kr(clk, 0.001, 1.5);
            let clk_patched = clip((clk_env - 0.02) * 100.0, 0.0, 1.0);

            // Granular eligibility for clock modes (must be > 0.02 to enter
            // the granular path; otherwise the whole-splice path runs and
            // CLK is ignored).
            let granular_eligible = clip((gene_size_n - 0.02) * 1000.0, 0.0, 1.0);

            // Morph 11:00 ≈ 0.46 splits the two clock modes.
            let morph_above_46 = clip((morph_n - 0.46) * 1000.0, 0.0, 1.0);
            let stretch_mode = clk_patched * granular_eligible * morph_above_46;
            let shift_mode   = clk_patched * granular_eligible * (1.0 - morph_above_46);
            let clock_mode   = stretch_mode + shift_mode;
            let auto_mode    = 1.0 - clock_mode;

            // --- Spawn trigger blend (Story D) ---------------------------------
            // Autonomous Impulse runs in auto_mode; CLK rising edge runs in
            // clock_mode. Lag on the mode flags so the crossover is glitch-
            // free (5 ms — same time-constant as the gene-size branch
            // crossfade and the spawn-rate "Dynamic Enveloping" lag).
            let auto_trig_ar = impulse_ar(smoothed_rate, 0.0);
            let clk_rising_ar = k2a_ar(clk_rising_kr);
            let auto_mode_ar = lag_ar(auto_mode, 0.005);
            let clock_mode_ar = 1.0 - auto_mode_ar;
            let spawn_trig = auto_trig_ar * auto_mode_ar
                           + clk_rising_ar * clock_mode_ar;
            let spawn_trig_kr = a2k_kr(spawn_trig);

            // --- Per-grain pan (C4) --------------------------------------------
            // pan_amount ramps 0..1 across Morph 0.55..0.85.
            let pan_amount = clip((morph_n - 0.55) * 3.3333, 0.0, 1.0);
            let pan_raw = white_noise_kr() * pan_amount;
            let grain_pan = latch_kr(pan_raw, spawn_trig_kr);

            // --- Per-grain pitch-up (C5) ---------------------------------------
            // pitch_amount ramps 0..0.8 across Morph 0.85..1.0. TRand returns
            // a fresh random in [0, pitch_amount] on each rising trigger and
            // holds until the next — already per-grain latched by definition.
            let pitch_amount = clip((morph_n - 0.85) * 6.6667, 0.0, 1.0) * 0.8;
            let pitch_rand = t_rand_kr(0.0, pitch_amount, spawn_trig_kr);
            let grain_rate = rate * (1.0 + pitch_rand);

            // --- Story D: Position advance for clock modes ---------------------
            // gene_dur in frames; signed step = +gene_dur in Time Stretch,
            // ±gene_dur · sign(rate) in Gene Shift, 0 otherwise.
            let gene_dur_frames = gene_dur_sec * buf_sr;
            let v_sign = sign(rate);
            let pos_step = stretch_mode * gene_dur_frames
                         + shift_mode   * gene_dur_frames * v_sign;

            // Stepper accumulates pos_step at every CLK rising edge; wraps
            // within [0, splice_len_frames). In auto_mode pos_step = 0, so
            // the accumulator is inert and the offset stays at 0.
            let pos_acc = stepper_kr(clk_rising_kr, 0.0,
                                     0.0, splice_len_frames,
                                     pos_step, 0.0);

            // Mix offset: auto mode uses Story A/C slide_offset; clock modes
            // use the Stepper accumulator. Lagged 5 ms to avoid clicks at
            // mode transitions.
            let mode_blend = lag_kr(clock_mode, 0.005);
            let mixed_offset = splice_offset * (1.0 - mode_blend)
                             + pos_acc * mode_blend;

            // --- Granular branch (C2) ------------------------------------------
            // Grain start position = splice_start + offset, expressed as a
            // fraction of the whole Reel (grain_buf_ar takes pos in [0,1]).
            let grain_start_frame = splice_start_frame + mixed_offset;
            let grain_pos_norm = grain_start_frame / buf_n.max(1.0);

            // grain_buf_ar(numChannels, trigger, dur, sndbuf, rate, pos,
            //              interp, pan, envbufnum, maxGrains)
            // envbufnum = -1 → built-in Hann window; maxGrains = 64 caps CPU
            // under 4× overlap with high spawn rates.
            let grain = grain_buf_ar(
                2.0,                  // numChannels = stereo
                spawn_trig,           // trigger (ar)
                gene_dur_sec,         // dur (seconds, per-grain)
                bufnum,               // sndbuf
                grain_rate,           // rate (vari-speed × pitch-up; pitch in stretch)
                grain_pos_norm,       // pos in reel
                4.0,                  // interp = cubic
                grain_pan,            // pan (per-grain via Latch)
                -1.0,                 // envbufnum = default Hann
                64.0,                 // maxGrains
            );
            let grain_lr = channels(grain, 2);
            let grain_l = grain_lr[0];
            let grain_r = grain_lr[1];

            // --- Branch crossfade (C6) -----------------------------------------
            // Gene-Size below 0.02 routes to the whole-splice path (cheaper and
            // bit-identical to a single-grain-per-cycle granular at full size).
            // The crossfade is a hard switch lagged by 5 ms to avoid clicks.
            let granular_active = clip((gene_size_n - 0.02) * 1000.0, 0.0, 1.0);
            let smooth_active = lag_ar(granular_active, 0.005);
            let mix_l = raw * (1.0 - smooth_active) + grain_l * smooth_active;
            let mix_r = raw * (1.0 - smooth_active) + grain_r * smooth_active;

            // --- Story D: EOSG (D1) --------------------------------------------
            // Per kb plan §6.D D1: spawn_trig delayed by gene_dur, then a
            // 5 ms gate, scaled to 10 V. Steady under Vari-Speed because
            // gene_dur_sec is in time, not samples (manual §3c).
            // Computed but not exposed — voice synthdefs return [left,right]
            // only; CV-output infrastructure for voices arrives with Story E.
            let _eosg_pulse = t_delay_ar(spawn_trig, gene_dur_sec);
            let _eosg_out = trig1_ar(_eosg_pulse, 0.005) * 10.0;

            // --- SOS RecordBuf (Story B, refactored) ---------------------------
            // Recording active iff sos > 0.001 (rec_active param dropped to
            // make room for clk). Forward-only at unit rate; loop=0 hard-
            // stops at end-of-Reel. The recorder Phasor is independent of
            // the playback Phasor so reverse Vari-Speed during SOS does not
            // flip the commit direction.
            let rec_active_internal = clip((sos - 0.001) * 10000.0, 0.0, 1.0);
            let rec_pos = phasor_ar(0.0, 1.0, 0.0, buf_n, 0.0);
            let in_mono = sound_in_channel(0);
            let sos_norm = clip(sos, 0.0, 1.0);
            let _rec = record_buf_ar(
                in_mono,
                bufnum,
                rec_pos,
                (1.0 - sos_norm) * rec_active_internal,    // recLevel
                sos_norm * rec_active_internal,            // preLevel (loop feedback)
                rec_active_internal,                       // run
                0.0,                                       // loop=0 (hard-stop at end)
                1.0,                                       // trigger
                0.0,                                       // doneAction
            );

            // --- Output --------------------------------------------------------
            // Synth-instance ASR keeps the synth alive for held notes; DC-block
            // each output channel.
            let env = envelope()
                .asr(0.005, 1.0, 0.02)
                .gate(gate)
                .cleanup_on_finish()
                .build();

            let left  = leak_dc_ar(mix_l * env, 0.995);
            let right = leak_dc_ar(mix_r * env, 0.995);

            [left, right]
        })
});

// =====================================================================
// Story E — Reel persistence: helpers + default-preset fill synthdef
// =====================================================================
//
// The Reel concept is a thin script-tier wrapper around `allocate_buffer`.
// The runtime's reload diff treats unchanged `(name, frames, channels)`
// tuples as no-ops, so the SC buffer is reused across hot-reload and any
// SOS-recorded content stays intact.
//
// Splice metadata is stored as a Rhai array on the Reel object map.
// `reel_attach(voice, reel)` wires `bufnum` and `num_splices` onto the
// morphagene voice. The synthdef divides the Reel evenly into
// `num_splices` regions today (see file header §3 + Splice model);
// arbitrary splice positions are a follow-up extension.

// One-shot fill synthdef. Writes a generated waveform (saw/square/sine/
// noise/silence) into `bufnum` via `record_buf_ar` with `loop=0` so the
// recorder stops at end-of-buffer; `doneAction=2` then frees this synth.
// Body args: 4 — well under the 10-arg Rhai cap.
//
//   preset:  0 → saw, 1 → square, 2 → sine, 3 → pink noise, ≥4 → silence.
//   freq:    fundamental of the generated waveform (Hz). The Reel is so
//            long that "fundamental" is more about loop period inside the
//            reel than pitch — pick something that gives a useful number
//            of cycles per Reel (e.g. 110 Hz × 8 s ≈ 880 cycles).
//   amp:     output amplitude written into the buffer (0..1).
define_synthdef("morphagene_reel_fill", |builder| {
    builder
        .param("bufnum", 0.0)
        .param("preset", 0.0)
        .param("freq", 110.0)
        .param("amp", 0.6)
        .body(|bufnum, preset, freq, amp| {
            // Mode-mix coefficients via cumulative-clip differences —
            // exactly one is 1.0 for any integer preset value.
            let m_le_0 = clip(1.0 - preset, 0.0, 1.0);
            let m_le_1 = clip(2.0 - preset, 0.0, 1.0);
            let m_le_2 = clip(3.0 - preset, 0.0, 1.0);
            let m_le_3 = clip(4.0 - preset, 0.0, 1.0);
            let saw_mix   = m_le_0;
            let sq_mix    = m_le_1 - m_le_0;
            let sn_mix    = m_le_2 - m_le_1;
            let noise_mix = m_le_3 - m_le_2;
            // (silence at preset ≥ 4 → all four mixes are zero)

            let saw_sig   = saw_ar(freq);
            let sq_sig    = pulse_ar(freq, 0.5);
            let sn_sig    = sin_osc_ar(freq);
            let noise_sig = pink_noise_ar();

            let val = (saw_sig * saw_mix
                     + sq_sig  * sq_mix
                     + sn_sig  * sn_mix
                     + noise_sig * noise_mix) * amp;

            // Write linearly from frame 0; loop=0 + doneAction=2 means
            // the recorder fills the buffer once then frees this synth.
            // Mono input writes channel 0 of each frame (mirrors the
            // SOS recorder in the main morphagene synthdef).
            record_buf_ar(val, bufnum, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0);

            // Silent stereo output — synthdefs need to return signals.
            [val * 0.0, val * 0.0]
        })
});

// `reel(name, frames, channels)` — allocate a persistent Reel buffer.
//
// Returns a Rhai object map with:
//   .name      — the script-side name (also the allocate_buffer key)
//   .bufnum    — SC buffer number, feed to set_param("bufnum", r.bufnum)
//   .frames    — buffer length in frames (float)
//   .channels  — channel count (1 or 2)
//   .splices   — Rhai array of normalized splice positions (0..1).
//                Initially empty; set with `r.splices = [...]` or
//                `r.splices.push(pos)`. Length is what gets written
//                into the synthdef's `num_splices` param by reel_attach.
//
// 8.35M frames × 1 channel ≈ 8 MB at 32-bit float — large but within the
// scsynth `-b 4096` script-buffer pool. For shorter loops, pick a smaller
// frame count (e.g. 480000 = 10 s @ 48 kHz).
fn reel(name, frames, channels) {
    let buf = allocate_buffer(name, frames, channels);
    return #{
        name: name,
        bufnum: buf.bufnum,
        frames: frames.to_float(),
        channels: channels,
        splices: [],
    };
}

// `reel_attach(voice, reel)` — wire a Reel onto a morphagene voice.
//
// Sets `bufnum` from the Reel's allocate_buffer handle, and
// `num_splices` from `reel.splices.len()` (clamped to ≥ 1 — a Reel
// without explicit splices is a single-splice whole-Reel reader).
// Returns the voice for chaining.
fn reel_attach(voice, reel) {
    let n_splices = reel.splices.len();
    if n_splices < 1 {
        n_splices = 1;
    }
    return voice
        .set_param("bufnum", reel.bufnum)
        .set_param("num_splices", n_splices.to_float());
}

// `reel_fill_preset(reel, preset)` — bake a default waveform into the Reel.
//
// Spawns a one-shot `morphagene_reel_fill` voice that writes a saw / square
// / sine / pink-noise / silence pattern into the Reel buffer, then frees
// itself when the buffer is full (doneAction=2 on the inner record_buf_ar).
//
// Re-runs on every script reload that calls this. To keep SOS recordings
// safe across edits, gate the call behind a flag:
//
//     let bake_default = false;
//     if bake_default { reel_fill_preset(r, 0); }   // or guard at app layer
//
// preset values:
//   0 → saw      (descending harmonics, comb-filtered grain texture)
//   1 → square   (odd-harmonic-only, hollow grain texture)
//   2 → sine     (single-harmonic — useful for clean "pure tone" baseline)
//   3 → pink noise (broadband — useful for granular texture without pitch)
//   4 → silence  (explicitly clears the Reel via near-zero amp)
fn reel_fill_preset(reel, preset) {
    let voice_name = "morphagene_reel_fill_" + reel.name;
    return voice(voice_name)
        .synth("morphagene_reel_fill")
        .set_param("bufnum", reel.bufnum)
        .set_param("preset", preset.to_float());
}

// .wav-backed Reels: keep the existing pattern from
// `examples/morphagene_loop.vibe` —
//
//     let reel = sample("reel", "samples/loop.wav").loop_mode(true);
//     let v = voice("morph")
//         .synth("morphagene")
//         .set_param("bufnum", reel.bufnum)...
//
// Pass `sample.bufnum` directly into the morphagene voice — the
// `.on(sample)` builder is shaped for `sample_voice`/`warp_voice` and
// would silently inject envelope/rate/loop params morphagene doesn't
// accept. Hot-reload re-loads the .wav, so any SOS-overdubbed content
// during the previous session is overwritten by the on-disk source on
// every edit. Use `reel(...)` + `allocate_buffer` (above) when SOS
// recordings must survive hot-reload.
